  "notes": "{傷|きず}つく is an intransitive godan verb meaning to be hurt, injured, or damaged.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive): {傷|きず}つく - to be hurt\n- ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive): ⟦{傷|きず}つける→傷つける：01935_kizutsukeru⟧ - to hurt someone/something\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{傷|きず}ついている: is hurt/injured (resulting state).\n\nUSAGE:\n1. Physical: {傷|きず}ついた⟦{動物|どうぶつ}→動物：01480_doubutsu⟧ (injured animal)\n2. Emotional: ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{傷|きず}つく (to be emotionally hurt)\n3. Objects: ⟦{床|ゆか}→床：03652_yuka⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{傷|きず}つく (the floor gets scratched)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{傷|きず}→傷：02201_kizu⟧: wound, injury, scratch, flaw\n- ⟦{怪我|けが}→けが：00787_kega⟧: injury (physical)",
